647a.5.5 0 0 1 .708.708L8.707 8l2.647 2.646a.5.5 0 0 1-.708.708L8 8.707l-2.646 2.647a.5.5 0 0 1-.708-.708L7.293 8 4.646 5.354a.5.5 0 0 1 0-.708"></path></svg></div></div><div data-rid="84293ebc-21d9-4d26-80a2-a25bb9585b8a" class="r-n4ae1q"><div data-rid="5dbfd049-cc0d-4523-8358-5dbaff37a5f1" class="r-1x2d2qp"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" role="presentation" style="width:var(--rsw, 100%);height:100%" class="r-13038l6" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M4.646 4.646a.5.5 0 0 1 .708 0L8 7.293l2.646-2.647a.5.5 0 0 1 .708.708L8.707 8l2.647 2.646a.5.5 0 0 1-.708.708L8 8.707l-2.646 2.647a.5.5 0 0 1-.708-.708L7.293 8 4.646 5.354a.5.5 0 0 1 0-.708"></path></svg></div></div></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="21d9a97a-10fd-4f54-8bd1-ae6ed2589561" class="r-daufr"><div data-rid="1ef4953a-a485-4ab8-a967-62b67fb554fc" class="r-rgdui5 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p><strong>Frequently Asked Questions</strong></p></span></div><div data-rid="7c3dbf93-2e9a-4bd2-a0df-2074826a0bd9" class="r-19sme4q" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="857d0e3e-aea6-4bd6-be12-dfede4af6ba8" class="r-3yaq5j" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="662c12ee-1ebf-4df8-b334-72c071d887e6" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:R1lr2:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-f2tzx8"><div data-rid="9570f5ee-6db6-44bb-8b65-02a6fa74cba8" class="r-1c5i0ay"><div data-rid="74ed6da2-8d0a-4de7-af26-8fe32b58121e" class="r-9kd79d alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>What is monthlies?</p></span></div></div><div data-rid="462d8499-18a1-4ef8-bd43-7e8a0ae86ab8" class="r-1e428h1"><span style="display:contents"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="feather feather-chevron-down" style="fill: none;stroke: currentColor;width: var(--rsw, 100%);height: 100%" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg></span></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:R1lr2:"><div data-rid="f7c22f32-4146-4ee6-a18e-478d38dca474" class="r-9mxd47"><div data-rid="9e519b4b-c6c0-4a3e-918f-44c3a7f7cbaf" class="r-shhllq alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Monthlies is a premium supplement that combines natural ingredients to support your menstrual cycle. You simply add one scoop to water once a day.</p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="f0f18ade-a519-4e7a-9989-be572d36213d" class="r-1dbwsi9" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="28666f6a-3e5f-4bbb-8f7a-1462e5ba7bee" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:R2lr2:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-ztcjwc"><div data-rid="bdf409ff-88a5-420e-86d7-3154a150a93b" class="r-6daxrv alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>What does monthlies taste like?</p></span></div><div data-rid="13b673ee-d672-4f2c-9136-b7d1a88fd51f" class="r-1atkw3u"><span style="display:contents"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="feather feather-chevron-down" style="fill: none;stroke: currentColor;width: var(--rsw, 100%);height: 100%" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg></span></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:R2lr2:"><div data-rid="2c4c9c49-b178-4b7c-aa25-e02f896bec65" class="r-nms02w"><div data-rid="d21245dd-0f98-4f25-aafb-d412df489700" class="r-1gsd8kp alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>monthlies has a tropical, slightly gingery taste. If it's a bit strong for you, you can try mixing it with more water and sipping it slowly. You can also add it to a smoothie or blend it into a cold beverage to make it easier and more enjoyable to take daily.</p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="0b1d8f8c-1356-464d-ab45-03e307b74553" class="r-xmcfko" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="9cf1c3ba-0f86-4ce1-8e87-fd8566389598" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:R3lr2:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-1nwb4n5"><div data-rid="ef56e4f5-572d-4952-bc5c-384f3d902941" class="r-1uf1imq alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Can I take monthlies if I'm using hormonal contraceptive?</p></span></div><div data-rid="484d2fde-e92a-4aa2-948e-e297f197b63e" class="r-rc1s5r"><span style="display:contents"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="feather feather-chevron-down" style="fill: none;stroke: currentColor;width: var(--rsw, 100%);height: 100%" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg></span></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:R3lr2:"><div data-rid="404ed40b-7b03-4677-91e7-da43f0a144d0" class="r-1pkxago"><div data-rid="5c018f67-c7f2-421f-8036-91956cf26c4e" class="r-kqyn2o alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>You can take monthlies while on birth control or hormonal contraceptive pills; however, it's essential to understand that the effectiveness of monthlies may vary since your hormones are already being regulated. Additionally, monthlies could potentially interact with your hormonal birth control. To ensure safety, it's always best to consult your doctor before adding any new supplements to your routine. </p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="a12d2a02-6f53-43b8-a3a0-9df1065757ed" class="r-ulb1w5" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="5dd5d071-5add-4908-8ca5-d7db24b934e2" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:R4lr2:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-1u2m4ew"><div data-rid="05b46c04-9bf0-43a3-ba03-f28af6a986eb" class="r-cz6m4x alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Is monthlies suitable for a teenager?</p></span></div><div data-rid="577fb505-ba67-4d5b-bbb0-a0ca33ac20f7" class="r-13qbeaj"><span style="display:contents"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="feather feather-chevron-down" style="fill: none;stroke: currentColor;width: var(--rsw, 100%);height: 100%" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg></span></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:R4lr2:"><div data-rid="fb698690-2f6e-4095-8514-1942e1498ab9" class="r-16qj30k"><div data-rid="7c78ec45-fb50-4d0f-8ec8-b25eee6c0793" class="r-1ys7fkx alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>monthlies is recommended for females above the age of 16, as this is when their menstrual cycle and hormonal system usually begins to stabilise. For teenagers under the age of 16 (18 in Germany), we suggest consulting a doctor before introducing any new supplement. While monthlies is formulated with science-backed vitamins, minerals and plant extracts that support menstrual health, it's always best to get individual advice for the teen's unique needs. </p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="e836fb24-0773-45c0-8639-3e39cc362716" class="r-1inv3rc" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="d7c19d07-2e33-47be-a609-b43f80be6217" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:R5lr2:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-1ooapui"><div data-rid="e13507be-3d02-4d3f-ad5d-ff67cb9781cc" class="r-1yahwkp alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Can I take monthlies if I have endometriosis?</p></span></div><div data-rid="f604ae31-be18-4b3e-9df3-237ce22d9dca" class="r-1713ngs"><span style="display:contents"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="feather feather-chevron-down" style="fill: none;stroke: currentColor;width: var(--rsw, 100%);height: 100%" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg></span></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:R5lr2:"><div data-rid="047f39fb-2b5a-490e-9062-5da2297aad9c" class="r-5em15p"><div data-rid="7616a8f2-8a8d-4de1-afa8-9c30080dc6cc" class="r-16ugfni alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Yes, you can take monthlies if you have endometriosis. While monthlies is not a treatment for endometriosis, it's designed to support menstrual well-being by addressing some of the underlying triggers of period pain, such a hormonal imbalances, prostaglandin overproduction and nutrient gaps. However, we always recommend you to check with your doctors before adding any new supplements to your routine and check for possible interactions with medications. </p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="73ca70e5-7b94-460b-9b9c-b081cd60407f" class="r-1uip3b0" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="7397389a-1bf5-4fa7-aca9-a8616811b95b" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:R6lr2:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-do79fq"><div data-rid="d2d7ffb6-46bd-4dcd-925b-34b8e272c533" class="r-1da36fg alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Can I take monthlies if I have IBS?</p></span></div><div data-rid="d6793ddd-644a-4fb4-b7f8-f4772a82669f" class="r-1t3f81o"><span style="display:contents"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="feather feather-chevron-down" style="fill: none;stroke: currentColor;width: var(--rsw, 100%);height: 100%" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg></span></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:R6lr2:"><div data-rid="7aa745f2-8663-4e81-b6f2-842e8efc8ca9" class="r-lhzitc"><div data-rid="785ec336-9c1e-48f7-8011-2a5fe9f7f8b6" class="r-19dovss alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>monthlies can be taken by those with IBS, but since IBS can involve sensitivities to certain ingredients, we recommend reviewing our full ingredient list before introducing it to your routine. If you're unsure about how your body might react, especially to certain dosages and ingredients, it's best to speak to your doctor or a health care professional who understands your condition. </p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="853ad231-5af7-4680-a5b8-c29f9f8cc872" class="r-1czv7rm" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="7c9d08be-6050-4c67-9c3a-6dba45cf0ea3" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:R7lr2:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-ddffk4"><div data-rid="f4711926-e799-430e-bcd6-efcfa1a14709" class="r-110bv6p alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Can I take monthlies if I have PCOS?</p></span></div><div data-rid="1d2368dd-3e5c-4b7b-91f4-a77059e57051" class="r-1iqvlk9"><span style="display:contents"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="feather feather-chevron-down" style="fill: none;stroke: currentColor;width: var(--rsw, 100%);height: 100%" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg></span></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:R7lr2:"><div data-rid="c543e66a-4272-4999-9daa-1183e88e30ca" class="r-rlr42a"><div data-rid="6a662a68-fa71-4342-a149-d81c00c0a5ce" class="r-10kg96o alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Yes, you can take monthlies if you have PCOS, as there are many ingredients that may benefit those with PCOS.</p><br><p>However, monthlies is not meant to treat any medical condition so you should always check with your doctor before incorporating new supplements into your routine. Please also check possible interactions with your medications (if any). </p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="747765f9-16cd-4754-98db-955d6bcb10c5" class="r-103c2mw" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="a6f309e3-7557-4ded-b8e7-236991debf55" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:R8lr2:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-x6ephn"><div data-rid="c97dda41-e55f-4301-b16a-e00c97b7473d" class="r-ed5jkt alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Can I take monthlies if I am breastfeeding or pregnant?</p></span></div><div data-rid="2ecad6ed-389d-40bb-8d1a-832ab1739914" class="r-raujtu"><span style="display:contents"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="feather feather-chevron-down" style="fill: none;stroke: currentColor;width: var(--rsw, 100%);height: 100%" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg></span></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:R8lr2:"><div data-rid="f0fb19b7-e0f9-49c4-b54c-0794622b3fba" class="r-b6ryuk"><div data-rid="64691f1b-b09f-4937-9aea-a2eb50a7e556" class="r-1qw9qi1 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>It is not recommended to take monthlies if you are breastfeeding or pregnant.</p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="82529a52-4179-428a-939c-e24fece45b88" class="r-esznyg" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="33bdd802-8b39-46d2-82e1-2fce06ff0a63" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:R9lr2:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-1dhd646"><div data-rid="722c5b56-2833-4e16-9c23-43700e5f4193" class="r-12b8re4 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>How can I book my free consultation?</p></span></div><div data-rid="04d89150-bcfb-4d0b-8c1d-479b76dde79b" class="r-aqmfs2"><span style="display:contents"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="feather feather-chevron-down" style="fill: none;stroke: currentColor;width: var(--rsw, 100%);height: 100%" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg></span></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:R9lr2:"><div data-rid="2ef10950-9039-4af5-9f68-649c58f92233" class="r-znv0df"><div data-rid="d6a3629c-16a5-4391-be7a-c3026cdee2aa" class="r-12tqr7b alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Once you've made your purchase, simply email us at <a href="mailto:hi@withmonthlies.com">hi@withmonthlies.com</a> with your order number and request a consultation. Feel free to mention your preferred time slots and any specific concerns you'd like to address. Our team will be happy to hep schedule your session and provide the support you need.</p></span></div></div></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="d21861e9-7156-4813-a46a-4d5ce1371e3e" class="r-1p5lrd6"><div data-rid="f6d81954-3090-4411-94d4-96318045c8dc" class="r-jzxneb" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="40d60407-2b61-4093-9ad2-dbec43c3e9ca" class="r-16tpjsr" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="132aa12e-d3f3-4e26-9172-518ec716b801" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:Ruj2:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-ddbbqs"><div data-rid="99ff9712-c340-4ff9-938a-c07094217199" class="r-9v3cgr alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Disclaimer:</p></span></div><div data-rid="866f8530-21bd-4dce-8c01-36deb36bce6d" class="r-1pomose"><span style="display:contents"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="feather feather-chevron-down" style="fill: none;stroke: currentColor;width: var(--rsw, 100%);height: 100%" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg></span></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:Ruj2:"><div data-rid="0759b3bc-b4c2-48aa-a14b-fd000f95f014" class="r-gdytif"><div data-rid="e1c8c6f6-5bae-46c0-9ab3-dc48839a829c" class="r-1dktkmq alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>The information provided on this website, through our products, and during consultations is intended for general wellness and educational purposes only. This product is not intended to diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent any disease or medical condition. The claims made here have not been evaluated by any regulatory authority. <br><br>Our health professionals and consultations are designed to provide general wellness guidance and should not replace advice from your healthcare provider. Always consult with a physician, pharmacist, or other qualified healthcare professional for questions regarding your health, medications, or specific medical conditions.<br><br><br>Important Information on Use: <br><br>1. Results may vary based on individual factors such as starting health, lifestyle, adherence to recommendations, and other unique circumstances.<br><br>2. Proper diet, exercise, and hydration are essential for achieving and maintaining health benefits.<br><br>3. If you are pregnant or breastfeeding, It is not recommended to take monthlies.</p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="018fbf00-9acc-4077-a63e-b1530edf6839" class="r-1kff0cx" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="c52b8f91-6306-4f8b-bf7c-5078b961fdcf" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:R1ej2:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-xfoa5f"><div data-rid="792669f0-4cb0-4aaf-9191-0a1ac7230501" class="r-11ru11g alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Study References:</p></span></div><div data-rid="8302df98-d80e-49b1-9a7b-01664eba8e1b" class="r-77k057"><span style="display:contents"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="feather feather-chevron-down" style="fill: none;stroke: currentColor;width: var(--rsw, 100%);height: 100%" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg></span></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:R1ej2:"><div data-rid="a6d16bb4-90d8-4cdc-bca9-ab0a596da6d0" class="r-m8u8wh"><div data-rid="9a518fc4-f1cf-46b5-8cad-e9d882b05d5f" class="r-11wlf2f alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>The impact of menstrual symptoms on everyday life: a survey among 42,879 women Harlow, S. D., & Park, M. (1996). American Journal of Obstetrics and Gynecology, 174(2), 683-689. https://www.ajog.org/article/S0002-9378(19)30427-2/abstract<br><br>NSAID Resistance in Dysmenorrhea: Epidemiology, Causes, and Treatment Options "A review of 51 clinical trials found that 18% of women report minimal or no relief of menstrual pain with NSAIDs." https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5839921/<br><br>NSAID use is associated with increased risk of acute kidney injury, particularly in older adults and those with chronic conditions. https://bjgpopen.org/content/6/1/BJGPO.2021.0208.long<br><br>Women with dysmenorrhea using NSAIDs had a 2.29-fold higher risk of stroke with prolonged use (≥24 days/month). https://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371%2Fjournal.pone.0259047<br><br>32% of women using NSAIDs for period pain reported gastrointestinal side effects, including nausea, ulcers, and diarrhea." https://bmjopen.bmj.com/content/14/6/e079660<br><br>Stanford University researchers found that ibuprofen use during ultramarathons doubled the risk of acute kidney injury compared to a placebo. For every five runners taking ibuprofen, one additional case of kidney injury occurred. https://med.stanford.edu/news/all-news/2017/07/pain-reliever-linked-to-kidney-injury-in-endurance-runners.html<br><br>Chronic Stress and Ovulatory Dysfunction: Implications in Times of COVID-19 Vigil, P., Meléndez, J., Soto, H., Petkovic, G., Bernal, Y. A., & Molina, S. (2022). Frontiers in Global Women's Health, 3, Article 866104. https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/global-womens-health/articles/10.3389/fgwh.2022.866104/full<br><br>Micronutrient deficiencies among women of reproductive age: a global and regional assessment Kothari, M. T., et al. (2024). The Lancet Global Health, 12(1), e76-e84. https://www.thelancet.com/journals/langlo/article/PIIS2214-109X(24)00276-6/fulltext<br><br>Houston, B. L., Hurrie, D., Graham, J., Perija, B., Rimmer, E., Rabbani, R., Bernstein, C. N., Turgeon, A. F., Fergusson, D. A., Houston, D. S., Abou-Setta, A. M., & Zarychanski, R. (2018). Efficacy of iron supplementation on fatigue and physical capacity in non-anaemic iron-deficient adults: a systematic review of randomised controlled trials. BMJ Open, 8(4), e019240. https://bmjopen.bmj.com/content/8/4/e019240<br><br>Ebrahimi, E., Khayati Motlagh, S., Nemati, S., Tavakoli, Z., & Hojat Yar, M. (2012). Effects of magnesium and vitamin B6 on the severity of premenstrual syndrome symptoms. Journal of Caring Sciences, 1(4), 183–189. https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4161081/<br><br>Fathizadeh, N., Ebrahimi, E., Valiani, M., Tavakoli, N., Hojat Yar, M., & Hojat Yar, M. (2010). Evaluating the effect of magnesium and magnesium plus vitamin B6 supplement on the severity of premenstrual syndrome. Iranian Journal of Nursing and Midwifery Research, 15(Suppl1), 401–405. https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3208934/#ref5 <br><br>Wyatt, K. M., Dimmock, P. W., Jones, P. W., & O'Brien, P. M. (1999). Efficacy of vitamin B-6 in the treatment of premenstrual syndrome: systematic review. BMJ, 318(7195), 1375–1381. https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC27878/#sec14 <br><br>James W. Daily, Ph.D., Xin Zhang, BS, Da Sol Kim, MS, Sunmin Park, Ph.D., Efficacy of Ginger for Alleviating the Symptoms of Primary Dysmenorrhea: A Systematic Review and Meta-analysis of Randomized Clinical Trials, Pain Medicine, Volume 16, Issue 12, December 2015, Pages 2243–2255, https://doi.org/10.1111/pme.12853<br><br>Rose, D. P. (1978). The interactions between vitamin B6 and hormones. Vitamins and Hormones, 36, 53–99. https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/217175/<br><br><a target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow noreferrer" href="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0708/7462/8371/files/studies_final.pdf?v=1731106438"><u>See all here.</u></a></p></span></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><style>@import url(https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Manrope:wght@100;200;300;400;500;600;700;800;900;950&family=Quicksand:wght@100;200;300;400;500;600;700;800;900;950&family=Lora:wght@100;200;300;400;500;600;700;800;900;950&family=Quattrocento+Sans:wght@100;200;300;400;500;600;700;800;900;950&family=Work+Sans:wght@100;200;300;400;500;600;700;800;900;950&family=Inter:wght@100;200;300;400;500;600;700;800;900;950&family=Domine:wght@100;200;300;400;500;600;700;800;900;950&family=DM+Sans:wght@100;200;300;400;500;600;700;800;900;950)</style></div>
